sections.wikitext:
* The song is used in the ending scene of the 1995 [[The Simpsons season 7|season 7]] episode of ''[[The Simpsons]]'' titled "[[Radioactive Man (The Simpsons episode)|Radioactive Man]]".<ref name="BBC">{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/cult/simpsons/episodeguide/season7/page2.shtml |title=Radioactive Man |access-date=February 27, 2007 |author1=Martyn, Warren |author2=Wood, Adrian |year=2000 |publisher=BBC}}</ref>
* [[Mary J. Blige]] performed this song on the [[HBO]] special ''[[We Are One: The Obama Inaugural Celebration at the Lincoln Memorial]]'' (January 18, 2009).<ref name="weareone">{{cite web|url=http://newsroom.mtv.com/2009/01/18/were-live-blogging-we-are-one-inaugural-concert/|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090119075819/http://newsroom.mtv.com/2009/01/18/were-live-blogging-we-are-one-inaugural-concert/|url-status=dead|archive-date=January 19, 2009|title=Live from the "We Are One" Inaugural Concert|first2=Gil|last2=Kaufman|first1=Erica|last1=Anderson|publisher=MTV News|pages=Entry titled: "Gil, 2:52 p.m."|access-date=June 6, 2009}}</ref> The next day, a crowd spontaneously began singing the song in the [[Purple Tunnel of Doom]] under the [[National Mall]] as they waited to gain entrance to the inauguration ceremonies for President [[Barack Obama]].{{citation needed|date=July 2026}}
* On October 3, 2015, [[Hillary Clinton]], during [[Hillary Clinton 2016 presidential campaign|her presidential campaign]], made a [[cameo appearance]] on ''[[Saturday Night Live]]'' in a comedy sketch alongside [[Kate McKinnon]], who regularly [[Saturday Night Live parodies of Hillary Clinton|parodied Clinton]] for the show. At the end of the sketch, the duo sang "Lean on Me" together.<ref>{{cite news|url = https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/hillary-clinton/hillary-clinton-tends-bar-impersonates-trump-snl-cameo-n438191 | title = Hillary Clinton tends bar, impersonates Trump in 'SNL' cameo | last1 = Sederholm | first1 = Jillian | last2 = Alba | first2 = Monica | date = October 4, 2015 | work = [[NBC News]] | access-date = November 24, 2019 | url-status = live | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20151005033049/https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/hillary-clinton/hillary-clinton-tends-bar-impersonates-trump-snl-cameo-n438191 | archive-date = October 5, 2015}}</ref>

sections.text:
* The song is used in the ending scene of the 1995 season 7 episode of The Simpsons titled "Radioactive Man".
* Mary J. Blige performed this song on the HBO special We Are One: The Obama Inaugural Celebration at the Lincoln Memorial (January 18, 2009). The next day, a crowd spontaneously began singing the song in the Purple Tunnel of Doom under the National Mall as they waited to gain entrance to the inauguration ceremonies for President Barack Obama.{{citation needed|date=July 2026}}
* On October 3, 2015, Hillary Clinton, during her presidential campaign, made a cameo appearance on Saturday Night Live in a comedy sketch alongside Kate McKinnon, who regularly parodied Clinton for the show. At the end of the sketch, the duo sang "Lean on Me" together.
